      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f42e5a54014a60529c7931e|full_name} \n\nFrom what I've gathered, all quality levels in the VRC Client appear to use Forced On prior to build 1440.\n\nVRC build 1400 (number might not be exact) added \"various performance improvements\" which changed the VRC Mobile quality level to use Per Texture.\n\nThe Editor quality settings have not been updated to reflect this, and still all use Forced On, which is out of sync with the in-game results.\n\nThis inconsistency has lead to many world developers who don't do extensive Mobile testing not knowing that they have to fix their Aniso Levels in order for their content to not be blurry, making the overall visual experience on Mobile noticeably worse.\n\nRegardless of my other conclusions, the current editor quality settings have Anisotropic Textures set to Forced On at all quality levels, so the quality settings are outdated regardless of if it was always Per Texture in the client.\n\nThere might be other inconsistencies I'm not aware of, too.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
